s</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">type</span> Event {
    eventId: <span class=3D"s">ID!</span>
    eventType: <span class=3D"s">String!</span>
    userId: <span class=3D"s">String!</span>
    properties: <span class=3D"s">[PropertyEntry!]!</span>
    createdAt: <span class=3D"s">String!</span>
    updatedAt: <span class=3D"s">String!</span>
}

<span class=3D"k">type</span> Query {
    event(eventId: <span class=3D"s">ID!</span>): Event
    events(eventType: <span class=3D"s">String</span>, userId: <span class=
=3D"s">String</span>,
        from: <span class=3D"s">String</span>, to: <span class=3D"s">String=
</span>,
        limit: <span class=3D"s">Int</span> =3D <span class=3D"s">50</span>=
, offset: <span class=3D"s">Int</span> =3D <span class=3D"s">0</span>): <sp=
an class=3D"s">[Event!]!</span>
    eventStats(from: <span class=3D"s">String</span>, to: <span class=3D"s"=
>String</span>): <span class=3D"s">EventStats!</span>
}

<span class=3D"k">type</span> Mutation {
    createEvent(input: <span class=3D"s">CreateEventInput!</span>): <span c=
lass=3D"s">Event!</span>
    createEvents(inputs: <span class=3D"s">[CreateEventInput!]!</span>): <s=
pan class=3D"s">[Event!]!</span>
    updateEvent(eventId: <span class=3D"s">ID!</span>,
        input: <span class=3D"s">UpdateEventInput!</span>): <span class=3D"=
s">Event!</span>
    mutateEvent(eventId: <span class=3D"s">ID!</span>,
        input: <span class=3D"s">MutateEventInput!</span>): <span class=3D"=
s">Event!</span>
}</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class=3D"code-label">EventGraphQlController.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">@QueryMapping</span>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> Event event(<span class=3D"k">@Argument</sp=
an> String eventId) {
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> service.getById(UUID.fromString(eventId=
));
}

<span class=3D"k">@QueryMapping</span>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> List&lt;Event&gt; events(<span class=3D"k">=
@Argument</span> String eventType,
        <span class=3D"k">@Argument</span> String userId, <span class=3D"k"=
>@Argument</span> String from,
        <span class=3D"k">@Argument</span> String to, <span class=3D"k">@Ar=
gument</span> <span class=3D"k">int</span> limit,
        <span class=3D"k">@Argument</span> <span class=3D"k">int</span> off=
set) {
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> service.find(eventType, userId,
        toInstant(from), toInstant(to), limit, offset);
}

<span class=3D"k">@MutationMapping</span>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> Event createEvent(
        <span class=3D"k">@Argument</span>(<span class=3D"s">"input"</span>=
) Map&lt;String, Object&gt; input) {
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> service.create(toCreateRequest(input));
}

<span class=3D"c">// method name =3D=3D schema field name; that's the bindi=
ng</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Every resolver delegates to the same <b>EventService</b> th=
at <code>EventController</code> and <code>EventGrpcService</code> call. Thi=
s is a third transport, not a third implementation.</figcaption>

    <div class=3D"callout" style=3D"margin-top:28px">
      <h4>Two places the schema bends to Java's shape</h4>
      <p><b>No map scalar.</b> GraphQL has scalars, objects, lists and enum=
s =E2=80=94 no dictionary. The domain's <code>Map&lt;String, String&gt; pro=
perties</code> can't be typed directly, so the schema models it as <code>[P=
ropertyEntry!]!</code>, a list of <code>{key, value}</code> pairs. A <code>=
@SchemaMapping</code> resolver does the conversion, and it only runs when a=
 caller actually selects <code>properties</code>:</p>
      <div class=3D"code" style=3D"margin:10px 0 8px"><span class=3D"k">@Sc=
hemaMapping</span>(typeName =3D <span class=3D"s">"Event"</span>)
<span class=3D"k">public</span> List&lt;PropertyEntry&gt; properties(Event =
event) {
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> toPropertyEntries(event.properties());
}</div>
      <p><b>No date scalar.</b> <code>createdAt</code> and <code>updatedAt<=
/code> are plain <code>String!</code> ISO-8601, matching how the app alread=
y serializes <code>Instant</code> over REST/JSON. A custom <code>DateTime</=
code> scalar is possible; this playground doesn't need one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 QUERY VS MUTATION -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">03</span><h2>Qu=
ery Reads, Mutation Writes</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">GraphQL splits every operation in two. A <code=
>Query</code> is declared side-effect-free and its fields may be resolved i=
n parallel; a <code>Mutation</code>'s top-level fields run strictly in sequ=
ence. In Spring for GraphQL that distinction is just which annotation the m=
ethod carries.</p>

    <div class=3D"tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Schema field</th><th>Controller method</th><th>EventServi=
ce call</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>event(eventId)</code></td><td><code>@QueryMapping e=
vent(...)</code></td><td><code>getById(UUID.fromString(eventId))</code></td=
></tr>
          <tr><td><code>events(...)</code></td><td><code>@QueryMapping even=
ts(...)</code></td><td><code>find(eventType, userId, from, to, limit, offse=
t)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>eventStats(from, to)</code></td><td><code>@QueryMap=
ping eventStats(...)</code></td><td><code>stats(toInstant(from), toInstant(=
to))</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>createEvent(input)</code></td><td><code>@MutationMa=
pping createEvent(...)</code></td><td><code>create(toCreateRequest(input))<=
/code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>createEvents(inputs)</code></td><td><code>@Mutation=
Mapping createEvents(...)</code></td><td><code>createBatch(requests)</code>=
</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>updateEvent(eventId, input)</code></td><td><code>@M=
utationMapping updateEvent(...)</code></td><td><code>replaceVersion(...)</c=
ode> =E2=80=94 ReplacingMergeTree</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>mutateEvent(eventId, input)</code></td><td><code>@M=
utationMapping mutateEvent(...)</code></td><td><code>mutate(...)</code> =E2=
=80=94 ALTER TABLE =E2=80=A6 UPDATE</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style=3D"margin-top:20px">Note that GraphQL's word "mutation" and Cl=
ickHouse's word "mutation" are unrelated, and this repo has both in one row=
. <code>updateEvent</code> is a GraphQL mutation that takes the cheap Repla=
cingMergeTree path; <code>mutateEvent</code> is a GraphQL mutation that tak=
es the heavyweight <code>ALTER TABLE =E2=80=A6 UPDATE</code> path. The tran=
sport doesn't change which ClickHouse pattern is in play =E2=80=94 only how=
 the call is spelled.</p>

    <p>One rough edge worth seeing: input objects arrive as raw <code>Map&l=
t;String, Object&gt;</code>, Spring for GraphQL's default binding for <code=
>input</code> types. <code>toCreateRequest</code>/<code>toPropertiesMap</co=
de> do by hand what Jackson does implicitly for REST's <code>@RequestBody</=
code>.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 ERRORS -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">04</span><h2>Er=
rors Ride in the Body</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">A syntactically valid GraphQL request returns =
HTTP 200 whether it succeeded or not =E2=80=94 there is no per-field status=
 line to hang a failure off. Errors appear in an <code>errors[]</code> arra=
y beside (or instead of) <code>data</code>.</p>

    <div class=3D"grid2">
      <div>
        <div class=3D"code-label">EventGraphQlController.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">@GraphQlExceptionHandler</spa=
n>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> GraphQLError handle(ResponseStatusException=
 ex,
        DataFetchingEnvironment env) {
    <span class=3D"k">return</span> GraphqlErrorBuilder.newError(env)
            .message(ex.getReason())
            .build();
}</div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note" style=3D"margin-top:8px">The same <code>Res=
ponseStatusException("Event not found: =E2=80=A6")</code> that <code>EventS=
ervice.getById</code> throws for REST is caught here and folded into the Gr=
aphQL envelope instead of becoming a 404.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class=3D"code-label">EventGraphQlControllerIT.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code">graphQlTester.document(eventQuery)
    .variable(<span class=3D"s">"id"</span>, <span class=3D"s">"00000000-00=
00-0000-0000-000000000000"</span>)
    .execute()
    .errors().expect(error -&gt;
        error.getMessage().contains(<span class=3D"s">"Event not found"</sp=
an>));</div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note" style=3D"margin-top:8px">No HTTP status is =
asserted, because none is meaningful. The failure lives entirely inside the=
 response body.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 THREE TRANSPORTS, ONE CALL -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">05</span><h2>On=
e Call, Three Transports</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">This repo is an unusually clean control group:=
 <em>create an event</em> is implemented three times, and all three impleme=
ntations end at the same <code>service.create(...)</code>. Everything that =
differs between them is transport, not behaviour.</p>

    <div class=3D"grid3">
      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">REST</span><sp=
an class=3D"tag">HTTP/1.1 =C2=B7 JSON</span></div>
        <div class=3D"tcard-file">EventController.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">@PostMapping</span>
<span class=3D"k">@ResponseStatus</span>(HttpStatus.CREATED)
<span class=3D"k">public</span> EventResponse create(
    <span class=3D"k">@Valid</span> <span class=3D"k">@RequestBody</span>
    CreateEventRequest request) {
  <span class=3D"k">return</span> EventResponse.from(
      service.create(request));
}</div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">Jackson binds the body into a typed record;=
 the URL and verb carry the intent; the response is always the full <code>E=
ventResponse</code>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">gRPC</span><sp=
an class=3D"tag">HTTP/2 =C2=B7 protobuf</span></div>
        <div class=3D"tcard-file">EventGrpcService.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">@Override</span>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> <span class=3D"k">void</span> createEvent(
    CreateEventRequestProto request,
    StreamObserver&lt;EventMessage&gt; obs) {
  Event event =3D service.create(
    <span class=3D"k">new</span> CreateEventRequest(
      request.getEventType(),
      request.getUserId(),
      request.getPropertiesMap()));
  obs.onNext(toMessage(event));
  obs.onCompleted();
}</div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">Overrides a generated base class; hand-maps=
 the proto message; replies through a <code>StreamObserver</code> so the sa=
me method shape supports streaming.</p>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">GraphQL</span>=
<span class=3D"tag">HTTP/1.1 =C2=B7 JSON</span></div>
        <div class=3D"tcard-file">EventGraphQlController.java</div>
        <div class=3D"code"><span class=3D"k">@MutationMapping</span>
<span class=3D"k">public</span> Event createEvent(
    <span class=3D"k">@Argument</span>(<span class=3D"s">"input"</span>)
    Map&lt;String, Object&gt; input) {
  <span class=3D"k">return</span> service.create(
      toCreateRequest(input));
}</div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">Bound to the schema by method name; input a=
rrives untyped as a map; returns the domain <code>Event</code> and lets the=
 engine trim it to the caller's selection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figcaption style=3D"margin-top:14px">All three return <code>Event</cod=
e>-shaped data from <b>EventService.create</b>. Only REST wraps it in a ded=
icated <code>EventResponse</code> DTO; gRPC converts to <code>EventMessage<=
/code>; GraphQL returns the domain record and resolves fields off it on dem=
and.</figcaption>
  </section>

  <!-- 06 THE COMPARISON -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">06</span><h2>RE=
ST vs. gRPC vs. GraphQL</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">The same seven questions, answered by the thre=
e controllers above.</p>

    <div class=3D"tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>REST</th><th>gRPC</th><th>GraphQL</th></tr=
>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Endpoint style</td>
            <td>one URL per operation =E2=80=94 <code>/api/events</code>, <=
code>/api/events/{id}</code>, <code>/api/events/stats</code></td>
            <td>one RPC per operation on a service =E2=80=94 <code>EventGrp=
cService/CreateEvent</code>, port <code>9090</code></td>
            <td>one URL total =E2=80=94 <code>POST /graphql</code>; the bod=
y names the operation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Request shape</td>
            <td>verb + path + query params + JSON body</td>
            <td>a single generated message, <code>CreateEventRequestProto</=
code></td>
            <td>a query document plus variables, validated against the sche=
ma</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Response shape</td>
            <td class=3D"no">fixed by the endpoint (<code>EventResponse</co=
de>)</td>
            <td class=3D"no">fixed by the message (<code>EventMessage</code=
>)</td>
            <td class=3D"yes">chosen per request by the caller</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Contract</td>
            <td class=3D"no">DTO records + OpenAPI, kept in sync by hand</t=
d>
            <td class=3D"yes"><code>event.proto</code>, compiled to stub + =
skeleton</td>
            <td class=3D"yes"><code>schema.graphqls</code>, enforced at req=
uest time</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Typing into Java</td>
            <td>typed =E2=80=94 Jackson binds to <code>CreateEventRequest</=
code>, <code>@Valid</code> applies</td>
            <td class=3D"yes">typed =E2=80=94 generated classes, no parsing=
 step</td>
            <td class=3D"no">untyped at the boundary =E2=80=94 <code>Map&lt=
;String, Object&gt;</code>, converted by hand</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Over-fetching</td>
            <td class=3D"no">yes =E2=80=94 <code>GET /api/events/{id}</code=
> always returns all six fields</td>
            <td class=3D"no">yes =E2=80=94 every client gets the whole <cod=
e>EventMessage</code></td>
            <td class=3D"yes">no =E2=80=94 unselected fields are never reso=
lved</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Under-fetching</td>
            <td class=3D"no">N+1 round trips for related data</td>
            <td class=3D"no">same, unless a bespoke RPC is added</td>
            <td class=3D"yes">one round trip; the query nests</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Errors</td>
            <td>HTTP status =E2=80=94 404, 400, 500</td>
            <td>status code in HTTP/2 trailers =E2=80=94 <code>NOT_FOUND</c=
ode></td>
            <td class=3D"no">always 200; <code>errors[]</code> in the body<=
/td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Streaming</td>
            <td class=3D"no">bolted on (SSE, WebSocket)</td>
            <td class=3D"yes">native =E2=80=94 <code>ListEvents</code> is s=
erver-streaming</td>
            <td>subscriptions (not used in this repo)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Tooling</td>
            <td><code>curl</code>, any browser</td>
            <td><code>grpcurl</code> via server reflection</td>
            <td>GraphiQL at <code>/graphiql</code>, schema-aware autocomple=
te</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Caching</td>
            <td class=3D"yes">free =E2=80=94 HTTP GET caching, CDNs, ETags<=
/td>
            <td class=3D"no">application-level only</td>
            <td class=3D"no">application-level only (every call is a POST)<=
/td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class=3D"grid3" style=3D"margin-top:28px">
      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">Reach for REST=
 when=E2=80=A6</span></div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">The consumer is a browser, a webhook, or a =
stranger. It is the only one of the three that needs no client library, no =
proxy, and no schema in hand =E2=80=94 and the only one that gets HTTP cach=
ing for free. <code>GET /api/events?eventType=3Dpurchase</code> is a URL yo=
u can paste into a chat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">Reach for gRPC=
 when=E2=80=A6</span></div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">Both ends are services you own and the traf=
fic is hot. Binary protobuf over a multiplexed HTTP/2 connection is the che=
apest of the three per call, streaming is native rather than bolted on, and=
 the generated stubs make a contract break a compile error instead of a run=
time surprise.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"tcard">
        <div class=3D"tcard-head"><span class=3D"tcard-name">Reach for Grap=
hQL when=E2=80=A6</span></div>
        <p class=3D"tcard-note">Many different clients want many different =
slices of the same graph, and you'd otherwise be adding a <code>?fields=3D<=
/code> parameter or a fourth bespoke endpoint per screen. You pay for it wi=
th an untyped boundary, no HTTP caching, and an engine that will happily le=
t a client write an expensive query.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class=3D"callout">
      <h4>What none of them change</h4>
      <p>All three controllers in this repo are thin. Validation, the Repla=
cingMergeTree write pattern, the <code>FINAL</code> reads, the ClickHouse m=
utation path =E2=80=94 every decision that actually matters lives in <code>=
EventService</code> and <code>EventRepository</code>, untouched by which tr=
ansport called in. That is the argument for keeping transports thin: it is =
what makes adding a third one a day's work rather than a rewrite.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 07 TRYING IT OUT -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num">07</span><h2>Ta=
lking to It: GraphiQL</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">With <code>./gradlew bootRun</code> up, <code>=
spring.graphql.graphiql.enabled: true</code> in <code>application.yml</code=
> serves an in-browser, schema-aware query editor at <code>localhost:8080/g=
raphiql</code>. It autocompletes against the live schema =E2=80=94 the Grap=
hQL equivalent of <code>grpcurl</code>'s reflection trick.</p>

    <div class=3D"gql-window">
      <div class=3D"gql-bar">
        <span class=3D"dot"></span><span class=3D"dot"></span><span class=
=3D"dot"></span>
        <span class=3D"gql-url">localhost:8080/graphiql</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"gql-panes">
        <div class=3D"gql-pane">
          <div class=3D"gql-pane-label">Operation</div>
<pre><span class=3D"k">mutation</span> {
  createEvent(input: {
    eventType: <span class=3D"s">"purchase"</span>,
    userId: <span class=3D"s">"user-gql-1"</span>,
    properties: [
      { key: <span class=3D"s">"sku"</span>, value: <span class=3D"s">"abc-=
123"</span> }
    ]
  }) {
    eventId
    eventType
    properties { key value }
  }
}</pre>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"gql-pane">
          <div class=3D"gql-pane-label">Response</div>
<pre>{
  <span class=3D"k">"data"</span>: {
    <span class=3D"k">"createEvent"</span>: {
      <span class=3D"k">"eventId"</span>: <span class=3D"s">"9f2c=E2=80=A6"=
</span>,
      <span class=3D"k">"eventType"</span>: <span class=3D"s">"purchase"</s=
pan>,
      <span class=3D"k">"properties"</span>: [
        { <span class=3D"k">"key"</span>: <span class=3D"s">"sku"</span>,
          <span class=3D"k">"value"</span>: <span class=3D"s">"abc-123"</sp=
an> }
      ]
    }
  }
}</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Note what is absent from the response: <code>userId</code>,=
 <code>createdAt</code> and <code>updatedAt</code> were written to ClickHou=
se but not selected, so they were never resolved. Drop <code>properties</co=
de> from the selection and the <code>@SchemaMapping</code> method from =C2=
=A702 doesn't run at all.</figcaption>

    <p style=3D"margin-top:24px">Underneath, this is an ordinary <code>POST=
</code> with a JSON body =E2=80=94 no client library required:</p>
    <div class=3D"code-label">the same mutation, by hand</div>
    <div class=3D"code">curl -X POST localhost:8080/graphql \
  -H <span class=3D"s">'Content-Type: application/json'</span> \
  -d <span class=3D"s">'{"query": "mutation { createEvent(input: {eventType=
: \"purchase\", userId: \"user-gql-1\"}) { eventId eventType } }"}'</span><=
/div>

    <div class=3D"callout">
      <h4>Tested without a browser</h4>
      <p><code>EventGraphQlControllerIT</code> mirrors <code>EventControlle=
rIT</code> and <code>EventGrpcServiceIT</code>: it extends <code>ClickHouse=
IntegrationTest</code> and runs against the same Testcontainers-backed Clic=
kHouse. In place of <code>TestRestTemplate</code> it autowires an <code>Htt=
pGraphQlTester</code>, sends documents, and asserts on response paths (<cod=
e>.path("createEvent.eventId")</code>) and on <code>.errors()</code> =E2=80=
=94 no hand-parsing of the JSON envelope.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHEATSHEET -->
  <div class=3D"cheatsheet">
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"section-num" style=3D"color:=
var(--mono-accent)">=E2=86=B4</span><h2>Quick Reference</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-dek">The six terms that unlock most GraphQL documen=
tation.</p>
    <dl class=3D"cheat-grid">
      <div class=3D"cheat-item"><dt>Schema (SDL)</dt><dd>The typed contract=
 =E2=80=94 every type, field and argument the server will accept. Here, <co=
de>schema.graphqls</code>.</dd></div>
      <div class=3D"cheat-item"><dt>Resolver</dt><dd>The function backing o=
ne field. Spring's <code>@QueryMapping</code>, <code>@MutationMapping</code=
> and <code>@SchemaMapping</code> all declare resolvers.</dd></div>
      <div class=3D"cheat-item"><dt>Document</dt><dd>The query text a clien=
t sends: one or more operations plus their selection sets. Validated before=
 execution.</dd></div>
      <div class=3D"cheat-item"><dt>Selection set</dt><dd>The braces after =
a field =E2=80=94 the list of subfields the caller wants. This is what make=
s over-fetching a client-side choice.</dd></div>
